WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:31.458
<b>In the previous verse,</b>

2
00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:36.250
<b>Lord Krishna explained how by </b>
<b>properly fulfilling one's duties,</b>

3
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.208
<b>a person can attain the highest</b>
<b>state of spiritual realization.</b>

4
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.916
<b>Now here, Lord Krishna is </b>
<b>giving examples of those who</b>

5
00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:47.708
<b>without attachment to the results,</b>

6
00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:53.083
<b>achieved spiritual perfection </b>
<b>by performing their duties.</b>

7
00:00:53.083 --> 00:00:55.791
<b>He is also telling</b>

8
00:00:55.791 --> 00:00:58.916
<b>that even after becoming </b>
<b> completely free from desires,</b>

9
00:00:58.916 --> 00:01:04.625
<b>what the purpose was of these individuals </b>
<b> who continued fulfilling their duties.</b>

10
00:01:09.583 --> 00:01:11.041
<b>Lord Krishna states that</b>

11
00:01:11.041 --> 00:01:14.333
<b>King Janaka and other kings like him</b>

12
00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:20.041
<b>attained spiritual perfection by </b>
<b>fulfilling their prescribed duties.</b>

13
00:01:20.041 --> 00:01:24.083
<b>They were all free from personal </b>
<b>desires and self-interest,</b>

14
00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:24.875
<b>yet</b>

15
00:01:24.875 --> 00:01:29.458
<b>they never abandoned the path of duty.</b>

16
00:01:29.458 --> 00:01:32.583
<b>The purpose behind doing so</b>

17
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:38.458
<b>was to establish such an example of duty </b>
<b>fulfillment that the masses would also follow,</b>

18
00:01:38.458 --> 00:01:40.500
<b>and everyone would know</b>

19
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:48.000
<b>how spiritual progress can be achieved </b>
<b>through karma yoga by renouncing attachment.</b>

20
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.791
<b>Lord Krishna wanted </b>
<b>Arjuna to especially understand</b>

21
00:01:51.791 --> 00:01:56.708
<b>that if he left the battlefield and </b>
<b>turned away from his duty,</b>

22
00:01:56.708 --> 00:01:59.000
<b>people would also be influenced by it,</b>

23
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.625
<b>follow it,</b>

24
00:02:00.625 --> 00:02:04.708
<b>and would not hesitate to abandon their duties.</b>

25
00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:08.958
<b>What would happen to a society </b>
<b>where people are not dutiful?</b>

26
00:02:08.958 --> 00:02:13.458
<b>Where doctors hesitate to </b>
<b>treat in times of dilemma,</b>

27
00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:18.458
<b>where soldiers refuse to protect the</b>
<b>state for their own comfort,</b>

28
00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:21.916
<b>where people forget their duty </b>
<b>as soon as difficulty arises.</b>

29
00:02:21.916 --> 00:02:25.833
<b>Won't such behavior lead to </b>
<b>the destruction of society?</b>

30
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:26.583
<b>Moreover,</b>

31
00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:32.375
<b>such thinking will distract people from </b>
<b>duty and attract them towards materialism,</b>

32
00:02:32.375 --> 00:02:36.500
<b>lead them away from responsibility </b>
<b>and only towards indulgence and luxury.</b>

33
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:42.625
<b>Even on a personal level, </b>
<b>this can only end in sin and hell.</b>

34
00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:43.583
<b>For this reason,</b>

35
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.250
<b>the people leading society</b>

36
00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:52.875
<b>should always set an example of devotion </b>
<b>to duty for the welfare of the masses.</b>

37
00:02:57.125 --> 00:03:01.875
<b>If a small or large pebble is thrown into a pond,</b>

38
00:03:01.875 --> 00:03:07.708
<b>the ripples that arise from it do not </b>
<b>remain limited to the point where the pebble fell.</b>

39
00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:09.500
<b>The ripples spread out,</b>

40
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.458
<b>influencing the entire pond.</b>

41
00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.416
<b>Similarly,</b>

42
00:03:13.416 --> 00:03:17.916
<b>the actions you perform, whether small or large,</b>

43
00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:22.958
<b>the ripples from them reach others </b>
<b>and influence them as well.</b>

44
00:03:22.958 --> 00:03:25.208
<b>Especially those younger than you,</b>

45
00:03:25.208 --> 00:03:27.708
<b>be they siblings,</b>

46
00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:28.833
<b> relatives,</b>

47
00:03:28.833 --> 00:03:32.083
<b>or colleagues, they observe your behavior, </b>

48
00:03:32.083 --> 00:03:37.041
<b>learn from it, and perhaps even get inspired.</b>

49
00:03:37.041 --> 00:03:41.000
<b>Your influence is not limited to just yourself.</b>

50
00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.333
<b>Those who understand this responsibility</b>

51
00:03:43.333 --> 00:03:47.458
<b>know that their life also shapes</b>

52
00:03:47.458 --> 00:03:56.583
<b>particularly the younger generation’s behaviour </b>
<b>and perspective of the people around them,</b>

53
00:03:56.583 --> 00:03:57.666
<b>For this reason,</b>

54
00:03:57.666 --> 00:04:04.833
<b> it becomes essential to fulfill your </b>
<b>duties with integrity and dedication.</b>

55
00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:10.000
<b>By doing so yourself, you inspire </b>
<b>others to do the same.</b>

56
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.250
<b>Moreover,</b>

57
00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:16.666
<b>by following your duties selflessly </b>
<b>without attachment to the results,</b>

58
00:04:16.666 --> 00:04:24.541
<b>you also become a living example, </b>
<b>that more than personal gain</b>

59
00:04:24.541 --> 00:04:28.958
<b>collective welfare and helping others is more transformative.</b>

60
00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:32.166
<b>You set an example for this way of thinking.</b>

61
00:04:32.166 --> 00:04:38.250
<b>The environment, the people around you, </b>
<b>especially the coming generation</b>

62
00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:41.500
<b>certainly has an impact of your behavior.</b>

63
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:47.833
<b>Whether this influence will be negative </b>
<b>or positive is in your hands.</b>

64
00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:49.208
<b>Hopefully,</b>

65
00:04:49.208 --> 00:04:56.625
<b>you would want to leave a positive imprint</b>
<b>of duty and responsibility.</b>

66
00:04:56.625 --> 00:04:58.291
<b>Think about it.</b>

67
00:05:02.833 --> 00:05:06.416
<b>In both social and familial situations,</b>

68
00:05:06.416 --> 00:05:13.250
<b>your conduct and actions are far </b>
<b>more impactful than your words.</b>

69
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:19.791
<b>When elders in the family or society demonstrate </b>
<b>responsible and compassionate behavior,</b>

70
00:05:19.791 --> 00:05:24.083
<b>it sets a standard for others to emulate.</b>

71
00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:27.500
<b>The younger generation adopts </b>
<b>those life values more,</b>

72
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:32.916
<b>which they see their elders </b>
<b>practicing day in and day out.</b>

73
00:05:32.916 --> 00:05:34.750
<b>For example,</b>

74
00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:40.500
<b>if an elder or loved one in the family</b>
<b>actively participates in community service,</b>

75
00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.250
<b>respects others,</b>

76
00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.541
<b>makes fair decisions,</b>

77
00:05:44.541 --> 00:05:50.083
<b>then without saying a word, they inspire </b>
<b>others to these life values.</b>

78
00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:55.000
<b>Such behavior evokes a sense of </b>
<b>mutual respect in others as well.</b>

79
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:55.958
<b>Similarly,</b>

80
00:05:55.958 --> 00:06:00.458
<b>when parents show dedication towards their work</b>

81
00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:04.791
<b>and resolve challenges with patience and grace,</b>

82
00:06:04.791 --> 00:06:09.166
<b>their children learn the importance </b>
<b>of these very qualities.</b>

83
00:06:09.166 --> 00:06:11.666
<b>Whether it is the family at a small level</b>

84
00:06:11.666 --> 00:06:17.708
<b>or society at a large level, </b>
<b>all people are interconnected.</b>

85
00:06:17.708 --> 00:06:19.458
<b>For this reason,</b>

86
00:06:19.458 --> 00:06:22.583
<b>the approach of keeping one's conduct pure</b>

87
00:06:22.583 --> 00:06:27.541
<b>not only gives birth to positive values </b>
<b>in the family and society</b>

88
00:06:27.541 --> 00:06:28.500
<b>but</b>

89
00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:32.583
<b>also instills sweetness in relationships.</b>

90
00:06:32.583 --> 00:06:34.083
<b> Moreover,</b>

91
00:06:34.083 --> 00:06:39.166
<b>such high demeanor of elders makes </b>
<b>the younger ones feel supported.</b>

92
00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:42.458
<b>They receive proper guidance.</b>

93
00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:45.833
<b>Your behavior is not just a personal responsibility,</b>

94
00:06:45.833 --> 00:06:46.750
<b>but</b>

95
00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:50.291
<b>a familial and social one as well.</b>

96
00:06:50.291 --> 00:06:52.000
<b>Think about it.</b>

97
00:06:56.500 --> 00:07:01.291
<b>The role of a person leading any </b>
<b>professional environment</b>

98
00:07:01.291 --> 00:07:06.916
<b>is not limited to just efficiently </b>
<b>completing personal work.</b>

99
00:07:06.916 --> 00:07:13.041
<b>True leadership also includes the responsibility </b>
<b>of developing the abilities and thinking of others.</b>

100
00:07:13.041 --> 00:07:18.416
<b>For a person appointed to any </b>
<b>leadership position, it is not necessary</b>

101
00:07:18.416 --> 00:07:24.458
<b>that they just provide solutions to </b>
<b>problems by solving them themselves.</b>

102
00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:25.625
<b>Rather,</b>

103
00:07:25.625 --> 00:07:27.375
<b>it is more essential that</b>

104
00:07:27.375 --> 00:07:30.666
<b>their perspective of looking at problems</b>

105
00:07:30.666 --> 00:07:36.375
<b>and their process of resolving </b>
<b>them are taught to their colleagues.</b>

106
00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:37.375
<b>Moreover,</b>

107
00:07:37.375 --> 00:07:39.291
<b>it becomes their responsibility</b>

108
00:07:39.291 --> 00:07:45.250
<b>to periodically observe the </b>
<b>working methods of their colleagues,</b>

109
00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.875
<b>provide appropriate suggestions,</b>

110
00:07:46.875 --> 00:07:52.041
<b>and give those colleagues opportunities </b>
<b>to learn and progress.</b>

111
00:07:52.041 --> 00:07:55.208
<b>If such a person wants people</b>

112
00:07:55.208 --> 00:08:00.791
<b>to work with dedication, commitment, </b>
<b>and a sense of responsibility,</b>

113
00:08:00.791 --> 00:08:04.541
<b>then it is only possible when they themselves</b>

114
00:08:04.541 --> 00:08:10.833
<b>consistently demonstrate these values through </b>
<b>their work and interpersonal behaviour.</b>

115
00:08:10.833 --> 00:08:17.125
<b>When senior officials spend their valuable </b>
<b>time for the growth of their team members,</b>

116
00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:21.375
<b>understand people's problems, solve them,</b>

117
00:08:21.375 --> 00:08:22.041
<b>and</b>

118
00:08:22.041 --> 00:08:26.583
<b>suggest a new perspective to </b>
<b>look at that problem,</b>

119
00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:31.041
<b>then all employees feel valued.</b>

120
00:08:31.041 --> 00:08:35.833
<b>Such employees will always come forward </b>
<b>to take on more responsibility</b>

121
00:08:35.833 --> 00:08:36.583
<b>because</b>

122
00:08:36.583 --> 00:08:40.625
<b>they know that if any problem arises,</b>

123
00:08:40.625 --> 00:08:46.541
<b>they will receive positive guidance, </b>
<b>not negative blame.</b>

124
00:08:46.541 --> 00:08:47.791
<b>Essentially,</b>

125
00:08:47.791 --> 00:08:51.208
<b>those senior officials who see </b>
<b>themselves not just as workers,</b>

126
00:08:51.208 --> 00:08:55.375
<b>but as guides for others,</b>

127
00:08:55.375 --> 00:09:00.791
<b>they will be instrumental in providing both </b>
<b>progress and stability to the organization.</b>

128
00:09:00.791 --> 00:09:03.666
<b>If you too are in such a position,</b>

129
00:09:03.666 --> 00:09:08.458
<b>then guide others with your </b>
<b>experience and example.</b>

130
00:09:08.458 --> 00:09:11.125
<b>Empower your colleagues,</b>

131
00:09:11.125 --> 00:09:14.000
<b>take interest in their progress.</b>

132
00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:18.791
<b>This will promote growth and </b>
<b>cooperation in the organization.</b>

133
00:09:18.791 --> 00:09:23.291
<b>And your own progress is included in this as well.</b>

134
00:09:23.291 --> 00:09:24.958
<b>Think about it.</b>

